---
import Vision from "../Vision.astro";
import stories from "../../data/vision-stories.json";
import Figure from "../ProjectFigure.astro";
import "../../styles/coastal.css";
interface Props { sourceNotes: string[]; }
const { sourceNotes } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="coastal-hero coastal-dark" aria-labelledby="project-title">
  <div class="coastal-wrap">
    <div class="coastal-hero-grid">
      <div class="coastal-hero-copy">
        <h1 id="project-title" class="project-display-title">{stories["robotic-block-assembly"].headlineLines.map(line => <span class="display-line">{line}{" "}</span>)}</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="coastal-hero-visual">
        <div class="coastal-image-label"><span>01 / Breakwater assembly</span><span>Concept rendering</span></div>
        <Figure id="breakwater" hero />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="coastal-section coastal-intro" id="abstract" aria-labelledby="abstract-title">
  <div class="coastal-wrap coastal-editorial">
    <p class="coastal-index">01 / Concept</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="abstract-title">Begin with a joint.</h2>
      <p class="coastal-body-copy">Before assembling a breakwater, a robot must connect one module to the next. The AMERICA concept starts with joint geometry: where to grasp a unit, how to align it, and which motion engages the connection.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="coastal-section coastal-method" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="coastal-wrap">
    <div class="coastal-section-heading"><p class="coastal-index">02 / Method</p><div><h2 id="method-title">Design for assembly.</h2><p>Connect the geometry of a module with the way it is made and placed.</p></div></div>
    <div class="coastal-materials">
      <article class="coastal-material"><div class="coastal-material-title"><span aria-hidden="true">[ A ]</span><h3>Module geometry</h3></div><Figure id="module" /></article>
      <article class="coastal-material"><div class="coastal-material-title"><span aria-hidden="true">[ B ]</span><h3>Material deposition</h3></div><Figure id="manufacturing" /><p class="coastal-reference-note">Fabrication reference from the source presentation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="coastal-section coastal-dark coastal-assembly" id="assembly" aria-labelledby="assembly-title">
  <div class="coastal-wrap">
    <div class="coastal-section-heading"><p class="coastal-index">03 / Assembly</p><div><h2 id="assembly-title">The connection<br />sets the motion.</h2><p>Joint geometry guides how a robot approaches, places, and interlocks each unit.</p></div></div>
    <Figure id="connections" />
    <ol class="coastal-sequence">
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Pick up.</h3><p>Grasp the module for placement.</p></div></li>
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Align.</h3><p>Orient the unit to meet the joint.</p></div></li>
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Interlock.</h3><p>Place or slide the unit into position.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="coastal-wrap" id="concept"><Vision project="robotic-block-assembly"><details class="vision-source-figures"><summary>AMERICA concept & source illustration</summary><Figure id="coastal-overview" /></details></Vision></div>

<section class="coastal-wrap source-section" id="sources" aria-label="Project source materials"><details><summary>Sources & media notes</summary><p>The page uses supplied project materials. Source credits and complete text descriptions accompany each figure.</p><ul>{sourceNotes.map(note => <li>{note}</li>)}</ul><p>The concept images are extracted from the original presentation. The manufacturing photograph is a fabrication reference; it does not establish production of the illustrated breakwater modules.</p></details></section>
